## COMPACT RUNTIME CONTRACT

Use these exact forms instead of reading harness source or spending a turn on
`--help`:

```text
bin/state add-hyp --agent N --card-id ID --hypothesis 'desc' --file path:func:line --input-shape 'shape' --guard-gap 'gap' --diagnostic bounds|lifetime|type|size|uninit|state --strategy STRATEGY
bin/state update-hyp --id H-... --status STATUS [--note NOTE]
bin/state add-note --agent N --hypothesis-id H-... --kind data-flow|guard|variants|decision|context --text '...'
bin/state show-recent --agent N --hyps 10 --runs 10 --claims 10 --notes 10
bin/state recent-tried --agent N --limit 40
bin/state explain-queue --mode MODE [--strategy STRATEGY]
```

Use the strategy assigned by `bin/state resume` (`S1`…`S8` or `REF`); do not
substitute the fallback default when the queue assigned something else.

- Before a parser/decoder testcase, run `bin/find-seed <file>[:<Function>]`.
- Testcases live under `{{ scratch_dir }}/` and carry native-comment headers
  `TARGET:`, `HYPOTHESIS-ID:`, and
  `CATEGORY: bounds|lifetime|type|size|uninit|state`; C/C++ API cases may add
  `HARNESS: harness.c|harness.cc|harness.cpp`.
- Different C/C++ harness logic needs a unique sibling filename per runnable
  testcase; put that exact name in HARNESS and never overwrite a shared harness.
- Run `bin/probe "{{ scratch_dir }}/<testcase>"` immediately; after a first
  diagnostic, run the same path with `--confirm`. For opaque bytes, preserve
  them exactly and pass `--hypothesis-id H-...`; under S8 add
  `--property <kind>`.
- If target code must generate, transform, or inspect a seed, perform that
  setup inside the testcase's `HARNESS` under `bin/probe`, never by invoking
  the target ad hoc from the shell first.
- Search target source with scoped `bin/rg-safe` calls, inspect ranges with
  `bin/peek FILE:start-end`, and view fixes with `bin/show-patch <commit>
  [path]`. Search artifacts with `bin/scratch-search`, not the raw log tree.
- Never kill by process name/argv: no `pkill`/`killall` (including absolute
  paths), and no `pgrep`/`ps`/pipeline/script feeding matched PIDs to `kill`.
  A target name also appears in concurrent cells. Signal only a PID you saved.
- Never read raw state JSONL or harness `bin/`/`lib/` source to rediscover this
  contract. Use the compact `bin/state` views above.

Every turn replays the conversation. Batch independent tool calls in one
assistant response, keep search/read output narrow, and checkpoint each
conclusion to `bin/state` as soon as it is known.

{{ turn_budget_section }}

The soft self-pacing targets are ~{{ tool_call_soft_target }} tool calls for
discovery and ~{{ tool_call_deep_soft_target }} for deep investigation. A
productive session should create or advance a hypothesis every ~30 calls.

Concrete security issues go under `findings/FIND-*` as soon as the report can
name a location, issue class, impact, and caller control; pure correctness is
not a finding. Promote a sanitizer-class diagnostic to `crashes/` only through
`bin/probe --confirm`. Reports use the bare labels `Boundary:`,
`Caller controls:`, `Trusted caller actions:`, `Caller contract:`,
`Trigger source:`, and `Strategy:`.
